  "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={5}^{u},\\,u={x}^{3}+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={5}^{u}ln\u2061(5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={5}^{u}ln\u2061(5)\\cdot (3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}ln\u2061(5)\\cdot {5}^{u} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}ln\u2061(5)\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
